# AI debug overlay + global theme — tool APIs of the Worker (DEVELOPMENT ONLY).
# Copy to `.env.local` for local dev.
#
# In production `/api/annotations` and `/api/config` answer 404 and production
# builds never call them (audit SEC-1): pins and the global theme are a
# development tool. The Worker turns them on only when TOOLS_API_ENABLED="1",
# which is set ONLY for `wrangler dev`, in `.dev.vars` (git-ignored) — never in
# wrangler.toml [vars] and never in the Cloudflare dashboard.

# Absolute URL of a LOCAL Worker started with `wrangler dev` (see below). Without
# it the overlay keeps pins in localStorage + vulcan-debug-registry.json only.
# VITE_ANNOTATIONS_API=http://localhost:8787/api/annotations

# Optional soft write-gate, dev only (never inlined in production builds).
# Must match ANNOTATIONS_KEY in `.dev.vars`.
# VITE_ANNOTATIONS_KEY=some-shared-string

# ── Local Worker + D1 (wrangler dev) ────────────────────────────────────────
# Production is a WORKER (…workers.dev), not Pages. The API lives in
# `worker/index.ts`; the D1 binding is declared in `wrangler.toml` and deploys
# with the Worker — no dashboard binding modal, no API token.
#
#   1. `.dev.vars` next to wrangler.toml (git-ignored), for example:
#        TOOLS_API_ENABLED="1"
#        # optional: CORS allowlist (default http://localhost:5174,http://127.0.0.1:5174)
#        # TOOLS_API_ORIGINS="http://localhost:5174"
#        # optional: ANNOTATIONS_KEY="some-shared-string"
#   2. Load the schema into the LOCAL D1 (tables `annotations` and `config`):
#        npx wrangler d1 execute vulcan-annotations --local --file=./schema.sql
#   3. npm run build && npx wrangler dev --local     (Worker on :8787)
#   4. Verify: curl http://localhost:8787/api/annotations → `[]` (JSON).
#      Without TOOLS_API_ENABLED, and in production, the same URL → 404.
#
# Production D1 (vulcan-annotations, id 471d2a9d-1a54-418e-849c-479b85cbd979)
# keeps the tables created earlier; the deployed Worker no longer serves them.
